+### [Distortion Loss](2755-distortion-loss.md)
+Distortion Loss is a regularization term used in differentiable volume rendering that penalizes uncertainty in depth estimation by encouraging the rendering weights to be concentrated around the true depth. It serves as a geometric prior that complements photometric losses, helping to resolve the inherent ambiguity in monocular NeRF optimization where multiple density distributions can produce the same color output. Unlike [Total Variation Regularization](860-total-variation-regularization.md) which smooths field values, Distortion Loss operates on the ray-space integration weights to enforce physical plausibility of the scene geometry.
+
 ### [L1+SSIM Loss](2890-l1-ssim-loss.md)
 L1+SSIM Loss is a composite photometric objective used to optimize radiance fields and 3D Gaussian splats by minimizing the difference between rendered images and ground-truth photographs. It combines a pixel-wise L1 error term with a structural similarity (SSIM) term to balance color accuracy with perceptual sharpness. Unlike pure MSE losses which can produce blurry results, this method explicitly rewards matching local structures such as edges and textures.
